From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 18 May 2026 17:37:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS DXMT: boot-time BC support log + present counter accessor
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two small additions used by the iOS Mythic frontend:

- supportsBCTextureCompression result is logged exactly once at boot
  (`[iOS DXMT] supportsBCTextureCompression = YES/NO`). On Apple GPU 7
  (A15, iPhone 13 Pro) this reports NO. CPU BC decoders would be
  needed for any title that uses BC formats — though Thumper appears
  to use vertex/SDF rendering and uncompressed atlases throughout, so
  this is informational, not blocking.

- New C export: `uint64_t mythic_get_present_count(void)` — atomic
  read of the existing internal counter (the same one driving the
  `Present #N` cadence log). Used by the SwiftUI FPS overlay in the
  iOS app, polled every 100ms for smoothed FPS display.

Madeira-commit: 1a8b9d7ee963dc6131f36b77a09a6803a5acc256
Rebased: clean
Class: madeira-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-24-dxmt-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 src/winemetal/unix/winemetal_unix.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/winemetal/unix/winemetal_unix.c b/src/winemetal/unix/winemetal_unix.c
index 2696f12..87783d7 100644
--- a/src/winemetal/unix/winemetal_unix.c
+++ b/src/winemetal/unix/winemetal_unix.c
@@ -312,6 +312,12 @@ static bool query_bc_support(void) {
     }
   }
   g_bc_supported_cached = supported ? 1 : 0;
+  /* iOS-Mythic 2026-05-18: one-shot log so we can see if A15+ supports BC
+   * natively (would skip all the BC decoder work). Fires exactly once
+   * per process — first call to to_metal_pixel_format. */
+  dprintf(STDERR_FILENO,
+          "[iOS DXMT] supportsBCTextureCompression = %s\n",
+          supported ? "YES" : "NO");
   return supported;
 }
 
@@ -1488,6 +1494,12 @@ static inline void mythic_log_present_cadence(const char *path) {
   }
 }
 
+/* iOS-Mythic 2026-05-18: exposed for SwiftUI FPS overlay. Reads the
+ * atomic counter on the calling thread (typically a 100ms Swift Timer). */
+uint64_t mythic_get_present_count(void) {
+  return atomic_load_explicit(&g_mythic_present_count, memory_order_relaxed);
+}
+
 static NTSTATUS
 _MTLCommandBuffer_presentDrawable(void *obj) {
   struct unixcall_generic_obj_obj_noret *params = obj;
